WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.564
Your terminal sessions

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.154
now fit in

00:00:01.966 --> 00:00:02.732
your pocket

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.520
Mitchell Hashimoto's

00:00:04.331 --> 00:00:05.168
new app Rex

00:00:05.003 --> 00:00:05.852
is live in

00:00:05.664 --> 00:00:06.489
the App Store

00:00:06.628 --> 00:00:07.618
It puts terminal

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.267
sessions from your

00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:08.644
Mac

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:09.977
Linux and Windows

00:00:09.788 --> 00:00:10.731
machines on your

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.887
iPhone and iPad

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.585
Sessions keep running

00:00:13.397 --> 00:00:14.352
on your computers

00:00:14.329 --> 00:00:14.882
so you can

00:00:14.694 --> 00:00:15.554
check on coding

00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:16.014
agents

00:00:16.156 --> 00:00:17.182
answer a prompt

00:00:17.076 --> 00:00:17.830
or approve a

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:18.927
command from anywhere

00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:19.894
then hand the

00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:20.555
pane back to

00:00:20.366 --> 00:00:21.085
your Mac

00:00:21.614 --> 00:00:22.580
It is free

00:00:22.392 --> 00:00:23.029
and needs a

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.866
Rex Server running

00:00:23.678 --> 00:00:24.739
on another device

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.177
which Hashimoto hints

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:26.920
is close to

00:00:26.732 --> 00:00:27.675
a full public

00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:28.253
release

00:00:28.782 --> 00:00:29.796
Full story on

00:00:29.607 --> 00:00:30.503
the dashboard
